  "answer_core": "Don’t grant Marcus 15% equity, a CTO title, and a board seat on Friday. Those commitments are too permanent before you know whether the partnership reduces or increases dependency risk.\n\nKeep the meeting direct and serious. Tell him there may be a path to major upside, but only after evidence. Define a short, structured sprint that tests whether he can deliver the platform work, whether that work actually affects revenue, whether team continuity and knowledge transfer improve, and whether his behavior fits the governance you need. Make clear what strong performance in that window would unlock, without turning the discussion into valuation math.\n\nAvoid both premature commitments and vague delay. Give him a real path forward, but one tied to demonstrated impact on the company’s health.",
